{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1927","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"E. Klever Permutation"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given two integers $$$n$$$ and $$$k$$$ ($$$k \\le n$$$), where $$$k$$$ is even."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A permutation of length $$$n$$$ is an array consisting of $$$n$$$ distinct integers from $$$1$$$ to $$$n$$$ in any order. For example, $$$[2,3,1,5,4]$$$ is a permutation, but $$$[1,2,2]$$$ is not a permutation (as $$$2$$$ appears twice in the array) and $$$[0,1,2]$$$ is also not a permutation (as $$$n=3$$$, but $$$3$$$ is not present in the array)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Your task is to construct a "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$k$$$-level"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" permutation of length $$$n$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A permutation is called "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$k$$$-level"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" if, among all the sums of continuous segments of length $$$k$$$ (of which there are exactly $$$n - k + 1$$$), any two sums differ by no more than $$$1$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"More formally, to determine if the permutation $$$p$$$ is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$k$$$-level"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", first construct an array $$$s$$$ of length $$$n - k + 1$$$, where $$$s_i=\\sum_{j=i}^{i+k-1} p_j$$$, i.e., the $$$i$$$-th element is equal to the sum of $$$p_i, p_{i+1}, \\dots, p_{i+k-1}$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A permutation is called "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$k$$$-level"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" if $$$\\max(s) - \\min(s) \\le 1$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Find "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"any"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$k$$$-level"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" permutation of length $$$n$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of the input contains a single integer $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 10^4$$$) — the number of test cases. This is followed by the description of the test cases."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first and only line of each test case contains two integers $$$n$$$ and $$$k$$$ ($$$2 \\le k \\le n \\le 2 \\cdot 10^5$$$, $$$k$$$ is even), where $$$n$$$ is the length of the desired permutation."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that the sum of $$$n$$$ for all test cases does not exceed $$$2 \\cdot 10^5$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, output "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"any"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$k$$$-level"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" permutation of length $$$n$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that such a permutation always exists given the constraints."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n5\n2 2\n3 2\n10 4\n13 4\n7 4\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n2 1\n1 3 2\n1 8 4 10 2 7 5 9 3 6\n4 10 1 13 5 9 2 12 6 8 3 11 7\n1 6 3 7 2 5 4\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second test case of the example: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$p_1 + p_2 = 3 + 1 = 4$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$p_2 + p_3 = 1 + 2 = 3$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"kind":"text","text":" The maximum among the sums is $$$4$$$, and the minimum is $$$3$$$."}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"E","problemCode":"1927E","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1927/problem/E"}